# Modules confirmed to contribute zero data-model classes -- stated fact,
# not a gap. Verified this session directly against pm4py source:
#
# - stochastic_petri/ (pm4py.objects.stochastic_petri): pure algorithm/
#   utility functions operating on petri_net objects (ctmc.py, tangible_
#   reachability.py, utils.py). `grep -n "^class "` across the whole
#   subdirectory returns zero matches.
# - yawl/ (pm4py.objects.yawl): no object-model .py files exist at all --
#   only an empty exporter/ subdirectory. `find yawl -name "*.py"` returns
#   empty.
#
# Per docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-24-ontology-first-restart-design.md's
# "Handling modules with no located reference": flagged explicitly here
# rather than silently omitted or forced through invented shapes.

@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://wasm4pm-compat.rs/shapes/stochastic_petri>
    rdfs:comment "No data-model classes -- pure algorithm/utility functions over petri_net objects."@en ;
    dcterms:source "pm4py.objects.stochastic_petri (ctmc.py, tangible_reachability.py, utils.py -- zero class definitions)" .

<https://wasm4pm-compat.rs/shapes/yawl>
    rdfs:comment "No object-model files exist at all -- only an empty exporter/ subdirectory."@en ;
    dcterms:source "pm4py.objects.yawl (no .py files under the package besides an empty exporter/)" .
